  // ---- spec-v52 wave 52-28 §4.5.28: Blue Cross and Blue Shield of Louisiana overlay (20 of 20) ----
  //
  // The twenty-second named commercial-payer overlay (after Aetna §4.5.7 through
  // BCBS Minnesota §4.5.27), and the seventeenth "Blues plans by state" overlay.
  // Blue Cross and Blue Shield of Louisiana (BCBSLA) is the dominant Blue Cross
  // Blue Shield licensee in Louisiana and one of the largest independent
  // licensees not already routed to an earlier bucket. Placed before the generic
  // 'commercial' bucket so a BCBSLA packet routes to its overlay; it is matched
  // only by its own definitively-Louisiana anchors (the plan name and the
  // 'bcbsla' acronym, which carries no substring collision with the earlier
  // 'bcbsal' Alabama or 'bcbsm' Michigan buckets), so generic 'blue cross' /
  // 'blue shield' and other Blues licensees stay in the commercial fall-through.
  // Per spec-v52 §4.5.28 these rules check the procedural completeness of a
  // BCBSLA prior-authorization packet against the plan's own published submission
  // requirements -- not against clinical coverage criteria (that is the
  // reviewer's judgement and the applicable Medical Policy's job). Each rule
  // self-gates on `bundle.payer === 'bcbsla'` (detected by lib/pa/payer.js) and
  // returns a vacuous pass with an explicit note on any non-BCBSLA packet,
  // exactly like the other commercial overlays. Every citation is anchored to a
  // public BCBSLA provider page, re-verified on the maintenance cadence in
  // docs/pa-maintenance.md (ledger source `bcbsla-precert`). The set mirrors the
  // earlier commercial families so the twenty-two overlays stay structurally
  // parallel and auditable side by side; BCBSLA-specific routing names appear
