  // ---- spec-v52 wave 52-42 §4.5.42: New Jersey Medicaid overlay (20 of 20) ----
  //
  // The twelfth per-state Medicaid overlay (after Michigan §4.5.41), and the
  // thirty-fifth named-payer overlay overall. New Jersey Medicaid is one of the largest
  // state Medicaid programs by enrollment. It gates on its own per-state bucket
  // ('medicaid-nj'), detected BEFORE the generic 'medicaid' bucket in
  // lib/pa/payer.js, so a New Jersey Medicaid packet routes to this overlay while a
  // state-agnostic Medicaid packet still routes to the generic 'medicaid' bucket.
  // The §4.5.4 state-agnostic Medicaid core (R-PA-MCD-NNN) keeps firing via the
  // isMedicaid(bundle.payer) predicate, so the core and the per-state overlay
  // compose on the same packet. Per spec-v52 §4.5.42 these rules check the
  // procedural completeness of a New Jersey Medicaid prior-authorization packet against
  // the program's own published submission requirements -- not against clinical
  // coverage criteria (that is the reviewer's judgement and the applicable
  // provider-manual section's job). Each rule self-gates on
  // `bundle.payer === 'medicaid-nj'` and returns a vacuous pass with an explicit
  // note on any non-New Jersey Medicaid packet, exactly like the other overlays. Every
  // citation is anchored to a public New Jersey Medicaid provider page, re-verified on
  // the maintenance cadence in docs/pa-maintenance.md. The set mirrors the
  // earlier families so the overlays stay structurally parallel and auditable
  // side by side, with New Jersey Medicaid-specific routing names where the program uses
  // them (the NJMMIS portal for submission, the advanced-imaging
  // utilization-management program for advanced imaging, the program's pharmacy
